mvn validate  -->  Checks if the project is correct and all necessary information is available (e.g., pom.xml is valid).
mvn compile --> Compiles the project's main source code and places the .class files in the target/classes directory.
mvn test --> Runs the tests using a suitable unit testing framework (like JUnit) using the compiled test classes located in target/test-classes.
mvn package --> Takes the compiled code and packages it into a distributable format, such as a JAR, WAR, or EAR file, in the target directory.
mvn verify -->  Runs any checks to verify the package is valid and meets quality criteria before installation or deployment.
mvn install -->  Installs the package into the local Maven repository, making it available as a dependency for other local projects.
mvn deploy --> Copies the final package to the remote repository for sharing with other developers and projects.
mvn clean --> Cleans the project by deleting the target directory, removing all files generated by a previous build.
mvn site --> Generates project documentation and reports.
mvn archetype:generate --> Creates a new project from an archetype (a project template).
mvn dependency:tree --> Displays the dependencies of the project in a tree format, which is useful for analyzing and troubleshooting dependencies.
mvn dependency:analyze --> Analyzes the project's dependencies to identify used and unused declared dependencies.